cealed hand options\n\n**Reason:** I currently have 5 pairs (T2, B2, B4, B8, B9) in a 13-tile hand, which puts me on a promising path toward Seven Pairs (24 points). Exposing a meld by Chi would eliminate this possibility and commit me to a standard 4-melds-1-pair structure with less scoring potential. Additionally, keeping my hand concealed maintains flexibility for patterns like Fully Concealed Hand (4 points) or Concealed Hand (2 points). My current hand lacks a clear winning structure with melds, so pursuing the Seven Pairs pattern is strategically superior.\n\n**Answer:** Pass"}
